# Question: does a daemon stop stop every container it runs, the one that
# obeys its stop signal and the one that ignores it, and leave no process,
# control group, root mount or library state of either on the host
# (spec-container-1-runtime AC-11, the container-stop-on-daemon-stop test)?
#
# A unit test cannot decide it: a whole-daemon stop closes the plugin's
# connection with no notice, and only the stop drain waits for the plugin, so
# what this asks is whether the real daemon's drain reaches the container
# plugin and the plugin's stop removes every trace of both containers on a
# real kernel.
#
# Method: two containers. probe runs the probe mode that exits at its first
# SIGTERM; stubborn (the test store gives the name its mode) records the
# signal and keeps running, with a stop timeout of 1 second. The daemon stops
# with SIGTERM. The probe's gone mode then waits for each container's control
# group, root mount point and library state to be gone, and requires the stop
# signal each one recorded; stubborn must also have ended at least its stop
# timeout after the signal.
#
# The store lives under /run, not in the test's work directory: in the QEMU
# guest that directory is on the 9p share of the checkout, and an overlay
# cannot take a 9p directory as its upper layer.
option=needs-linux:caps=sys-admin
option=exclusive:group=container
option=timeout:value=150s
option=env:var=ze.test.container.store:value=/run/ze-container-test-$PORT

stdin=config:terminator=EOF_CONFIG
container {
	instance probe {
	}
	instance stubborn {
		stop-timeout 1;
	}
}
EOF_CONFIG

cmd=foreground:seq=1:exec=ze-containerprobe reset /run/ze-container-test-$PORT:exit=0
cmd=background:seq=2:exec=ze -:stdin=config:name=daemon
cmd=foreground:seq=3:exec=ze-containerprobe verify /run/ze-container-test-$PORT probe:timeout=45s:exit=0
cmd=foreground:seq=4:exec=ze-containerprobe verify /run/ze-container-test-$PORT stubborn:timeout=45s:exit=0
cmd=stop:seq=5:name=daemon:signal=term
cmd=foreground:seq=6:exec=ze-containerprobe gone /run/ze-container-test-$PORT probe:timeout=50s:exit=0
cmd=foreground:seq=7:exec=ze-containerprobe gone /run/ze-container-test-$PORT stubborn at-least 1:timeout=50s:exit=0
expect=stdout:contains=probe: its control group is gone
expect=stdout:contains=probe: its root mount is gone
expect=stdout:contains=probe: its runtime library state is gone
expect=stdout:contains=probe: the container received a stop signal
expect=stdout:contains=probe: it ended at least 1s after its stop signal
reject=stdout:contains=probe: FAIL
